---
import { REPO_URL } from '../consts';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const doc = (path: string) => `${REPO_URL}/blob/develop/docs/${path}`;
---

<Layout title="About" description="What this project is and how it is built.">
	<article class="about">
		<h1>About this project</h1>
		<p class="about__lede">
			Catan Tracker is my project for CS4421 DevOps at the University of Limerick. The scoreboard is
			the product, but the point is the engineering around it: code that stays easy to change,
			checks that catch mistakes before they merge, and a deploy that can be repeated, watched and
			rolled back.
		</p>

		<h2>What happens on every pull request</h2>
		<ol>
			<li>Commit messages are checked against Conventional Commits.</li>
			<li>Lint, type checks and the architecture rules run.</li>
			<li>Unit, property-based and browser tests run.</li>
			<li>The site, the container image and the AWS infrastructure are built and tested.</li>
		</ol>
		<p>
			Branches follow GitFlow. Features merge into <code>develop</code> through pull requests, and
			releases go to <code>main</code>, where release-please writes the changelog and the version
			tag. Mutation testing runs weekly to check that the tests really catch bugs.
		</p>

		<h2>Read more</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><a href={doc('architecture.md')}>Architecture overview</a></li>
			<li><a href={`${REPO_URL}/tree/develop/docs/adr`}>Architecture decision records</a></li>
			<li><a href={doc('handbook.md')}>Developer handbook</a></li>
			<li><a href={REPO_URL}>Source code</a></li>
		</ul>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.about {
		max-width: var(--prose-width);
	}
	.about__lede {
		font-size: var(--text-l);
		color: var(--color-ink-muted);
	}
	.about h2 {
		margin-top: var(--space-6);
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
	}
	.about li {
		margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
	}
</style>
